# .jacignore -- modules excluded from the repo-wide `jac check` gate.
#
# CI feeds every non-comment line here to `jac check --ignore` (see
# .github/workflows/ci.yml, "Run jac check (using .jacignore)"). CI adds
# `tests checker_*.jac *_err.jac` of its own; those are not listed here.
#
# Matching (jac0core/helpers.jac:path_matches_exclude): an entry containing
# `/` is fnmatched against the whole path; a bare entry is fnmatched against
# EVERY path component, so a bare `types.jac` silences every file of that
# basename repo-wide. Every entry below is path-qualified for that reason --
# one line per excluded module, so a fix deletes exactly one line.
#
# Each entry is a module that does not currently pass `jac check`. Adding to
# this list is a debt, not a policy: the goal is an empty file.

# Fetched at build time, not repo source.
# `jac ninja` fetches third-party zig packages into jac/zig-pkg/ and the
# tree-sitter-jac package ships its own examples/sample.jac. Bare name so
# any zig-pkg path component is skipped.
zig-pkg

# llvmlite-bound native IR generation.
# The NaIRGen* mixins reach llvmlite handles (ir.Function.args, .linkage,
# IRBuilder.append_basic_block, Type.as_pointer) through the vendored
# py2jac translation under passes/native/llvm/, whose ctypes-derived
# values the checker sees as Unknown. Not annotatable without typing that
# vendored surface.
jac/jaclang/compiler/passes/native/na_ir_gen/*

# Native compile driver (same llvmlite boundary as na_ir_gen).
jac/jaclang/compiler/passes/native/impl/na_compile_pass.impl.jac
jac/jaclang/compiler/passes/native/na_compile_pass.jac

# byllm -- litellm/LLM-provider glue.
jac/jaclang/byllm/llm.impl/basellm.impl.jac
jac/jaclang/byllm/llm.impl/local.impl.jac
jac/jaclang/byllm/llm.impl/mockllm.impl.jac
jac/jaclang/byllm/llm.impl/model.impl.jac
jac/jaclang/byllm/llm.impl/modelpool.impl.jac
jac/jaclang/byllm/llm.jac
jac/jaclang/byllm/telemetry.impl/telemetry.impl.jac
jac/jaclang/byllm/telemetry.jac
jac/jaclang/byllm/types.jac

